title Local runtime topology (consumer/compose.yaml + docker-compose.e2e.yml)

left to right direction

actor Browser as browser

node "Docker Compose network" {
    node "frontend\n(nginx, host :4443)" as frontend {
        artifact "Angular bundle" as angular
    }
    node "bff\n(Spring Boot, host :8080)" as bff
    node "fineract\n(Fineract Core 1.12.1,\nhost :8888 -> :8080)" as fineract
    database "bff-db\n(PostgreSQL, host :5432)" as bffdb
    database "fineract-db\n(PostgreSQL, host :5433)" as fineractdb
    database "valkey\n(Valkey 8, host :6379)" as valkey
    node "mailpit\n(dev SMTP, host :8025 UI / :1025 SMTP)" as mailpit
}

browser --> frontend : HTTP :4443\nstatic app + /api/*
frontend --> bff : proxy /api/ -> bff:8080\n(X-Forwarded-* headers)
bff --> fineract : Feign, service account\nhttp://fineract:8080/fineract-provider/api
bff --> bffdb : JDBC\nusers, refresh tokens, consents, audit
bff --> valkey : JWT denylist, OTP hashes,\nrate-limit counters, ownership cache
bff --> mailpit : SMTP :1025\nOTP emails
fineract --> fineractdb : JDBC\ntenant database

note bottom of frontend
  e2e stack only (docker-compose.e2e.yml).
  Backend-only runs hit the BFF
  directly on localhost:8080.
end note

@enduml
